# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Studio's OWN env file. It does not read the repo-root .env.
#
# Sanity's bundler only exposes the SANITY_STUDIO_* prefix and only reads .env
# files from this directory, which is why these two live here and not with the
# other nine. Copy to studio/.env.
#
# The project id, dataset and API version are NOT here — they are public and
# stable, so they sit in studio/sanity.project.ts. See the comment in that file.
#
# Both vars below exist only for the "Fetch media" button on a bird document.
# Everything else in the Studio works without them.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the button POSTs. The site route does the licence filtering, the
# downloading and the asset upload — the button itself is a fetch and nothing
# more (studio/actions/fetchMedia.ts).
#
# Defaults to http://localhost:4321/api/fetch-media when unset, which is only
# ever right on your own machine with `pnpm dev` running. A DEPLOYED Studio with
# this unset posts to whatever is on the operator's own localhost, so set it to
# the deployed site for any Studio that is not running locally.
SANITY_STUDIO_MEDIA_ENDPOINT="http://localhost:4321/api/fetch-media"

# Must be the SAME VALUE as MEDIA_FETCH_SECRET in the repo-root .env — it is
# sent as the x-media-secret header and compared there. Unset, it is sent empty
# and the endpoint answers 401 "Not authorised", which is the failure you get if
# you only set one of the pair.
SANITY_STUDIO_MEDIA_SECRET=""
